From ddf8e966e522d9fd0bfc09b37e8992d9b44e1922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(boundary): OB-3 one pending authority + binding
 convergence

- One pending-response record: the spine's ownership.expectedReply, extended
  with bindKey / offeredAtTurn / heldThroughTurn / optional / items /
  authority. Thin accessors (arm / held / release / read), no new store.
- Boundary reads it as plain pre-turn data (pendingOwnerSnapshot); one
  resolvePendingBinding per turn (Boundary meaning + permitsFor) decides
  what a reply binds to: bind / release / preserve / ask_which / none.
- Freshness by provenance: offer or a later person-before-process hold on
  the previous turn; a newer arm replaces the older offer.
- 19 bind sites converged (invites, Compass, acceptance dispatch, Create
  consent, frictionless/Strategy/avatar/Collection/VTS/handoff/survey,
  Decision Ledger, both Remember binders, frictionless yes-continuation).
- Model text can no longer arm executable authority.
- Decision Ledger B-10 reproduced and routed through the shared binding.
- Structural deferral family in the Boundary lexicon (OB-2R Events gap).
- Reconciliation rule 3: a HIGH acceptance bound to the live offer is not
  a topic switch. Divergence 4/285 -> 2/285 (only OB-4 receipt cells).
- Certification: pendingBinding.ob3 (85 production-path cases), OB3 corpus
  additions, OB-3 divergence baseline, consumer structure rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
